data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"# Assessment — dev d002 accepted\\n\\n## What was judged\\ndev's reply to d002 claimed: `src/greet.py` + `tests/test_greet.py` delivered,\\n`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0, committed as `ece8bfe` on\\n`cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`.\\n\\n## How it was judged (branch fetched, report not trusted)\\n- Fetched `refs/remotes/campaign/dev/subject`; head `ece8bfe`, tree differs\\n  from base `8ac1a36` (2 files, +25 lines).\\n- Read both files from the branch:\\n  - `src/greet.py`: `greet(name)` returns `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"` — matches spec\\n    exactly, including `greet(\\\"\\\")` -\u003e `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`.\\n  - `tests/test_greet.py`: two `unittest` cases — normal name (`\\\"Ada\\\"`) and\\n    the empty string; inserts `\u003croot\u003e/src` into `sys.path` so the import works\\n    under discovery from the repo root.\\n- Checked out the branch in a detached worktree and ran\\n  `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` from the repo root: **2 tests ran,\\n  OK, exit code 0**.\\n\\n## Verdict\\nAll three mission criteria satisfied on the first attempt. Accepted d002.\\nNo risks outstanding; fleet has spare capacity. Campaign is ready to conclude\\nas campaign-met.\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/assessment-d002.md\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_32","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1787461725,"id":"chatcmpl-d55b4a9bbbb645e396e72dc24b4059b2","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

